#!/bin/sh
# Build PractRand's own RNG_test from the archive pinned in
# src/practrand/PROVENANCE, unpatched, into the directory given. Run from the
# package root. tools/equivalence/compare.R tests pract_test() against it.
set -eu

OUT=${1:?usage: tools/equivalence/build-rng-test <out-dir>}
PROV="src/practrand/PROVENANCE"
URL=$(awk '/^  Archive:/ {print $2}' "$PROV")
EXPECTED=$(awk '/^  SHA-256:/ {print $2}' "$PROV")
CXX=${CXX:-c++}

mkdir -p "$OUT"
WORK=$(mktemp -d)
trap 'rm -rf "$WORK"' EXIT

curl -fsSL --retry 3 --retry-delay 2 --retry-connrefused \
  -o "$WORK/practrand.zip" "$URL"
ACTUAL=$(shasum -a 256 "$WORK/practrand.zip" | cut -d' ' -f1)
if [ "$ACTUAL" != "$EXPECTED" ]; then
  echo "FAIL: archive sha256 mismatch ($ACTUAL)" >&2
  exit 1
fi
unzip -q "$WORK/practrand.zip" -d "$WORK/x"
SRC="$WORK/x/PractRand"
find "$SRC" -type f -exec perl -pi -e 's/\r$//' {} +

# The whole library, RNGs/other/ included, as RNG_test needs it.
$CXX -std=gnu++17 -O2 -w -pthread -I"$SRC/include" -o "$OUT/RNG_test" \
  "$SRC/tools/RNG_test.cpp" "$SRC"/src/*.cpp "$SRC"/src/RNGs/*.cpp \
  "$SRC"/src/RNGs/other/*.cpp
echo "==> built $OUT/RNG_test"
